dArkOS RG52 Mini - NPU UPSCALE: third-party components
=======================================================

NPU UPSCALE enlarges an emulator's native frame with a small neural network on the RK3562's
NPU, inside dArkOS's Vulkan rotate layer (VK_LAYER_DARKOS_rotate). It uses:

1. librknnrt.so - Rockchip RKNN runtime 2.5.0
   Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
   Under the License Agreement for RKNN Software Development Kit Package (its full text is
   /usr/share/doc/librknnrt/LICENSE, npusr/LICENSE.rknn in the dArkOS sources, from the same
   release): for applications compatible with Rockchip's products (1.1), its notices kept
   (2.1(b)). dArkOS uses it only on the RK3562 of the RG52 Mini. Unmodified, as
   published in https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2 at the tag v2.5.0,
   rknpu2/runtime/Linux/librknn_api/aarch64/librknnrt.so
   sha256 4b6cc575bedf8952b13db4b1190fa3b3d2ac213f00be774ff6ccd19d651970c0
   Installed as /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/librknnrt.so; loaded by the layer only when a game
   starts with NPU UPSCALE on.

2. rknn_api.h - the runtime's header, from the same release and under the same license
   (vk-rotate-layer/rknn_api.h in the dArkOS sources; LICENSE.rknn beside it).

3. ESPCN x2 and x3, TF-ESPCN by Fanny Monori, https://github.com/fannymonori/TF-ESPCN (the
   models OpenCV's dnn_superres module uses), Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-TF-ESPCN, installed
   beside this file). The teacher both of item 4's models learned from: they were trained to
   give what ESPCN gives. ESPCN_x2.pb and ESPCN_x3.pb (TF-ESPCN's export/ files) are kept in
   npusr/models/ in the dArkOS sources, with make_espcn.py, which makes ESPCN itself into a
   model for the NPU (its first layer rebuilt as five rows; NPU UPSCALE ran on it before item
   4's models, and the layer still takes such a model).

4. The models, /usr/share/darkos/npusr/espcn_x3_400x240.rknn (the 3DS's, x3 from 400x240),
   espcn_x3_480x272.rknn (the PSP's, x3 from 480x272: the same network as the 3DS's) and
   espcn_x2_480x272.rknn (the PSP's with PPSSPP's integer scale, x2) - the file names the layer
   looks for; the networks are not ESPCN. Made for dArkOS in 2026.
   Space-to-depth networks: 4 luma channels of a 2x2 cell in, 3x3 convolutions of 32 channels
   (the 3DS's 9 of them, 76 324 weights; the PSP's 7, 52 048 weights), 1.7 and 2.4 times faster
   than ESPCN on the NPU. Their weights started from a bicubic interpolation written into the
   network plus random noise (seed 0) - no other network's weights - and were trained to give
   what ESPCN (item 3) gives on the same inputs: screenshots of PSP and 3DS games taken on the
   console; scikit-image's sample photographs (skimage.data: astronaut, coffee, chelsea,
   rocket, camera, coins, moon, page, text - public domain or CC0 by their notes there; moon
   and page have no note of their own and come with scikit-image under its BSD-3-Clause
   license); shapes, text and textures the training script draws. No image dataset. The 3DS's
   was then trained on with quantisation noise. Quantised to INT8 with rknn-toolkit2 2.5.0,
   calibrated on 3DS screenshots (10 distinct frames; the PSP's x3 and x2 on PSP ones, 15).
   In the dArkOS sources: npusr/models/s2d_distill.py trains them, s2d_rknn.py makes the
   .rknn files from their weights (s2d_x3_b7.pt, s2d_x2_v7.pt, kept there: training on a GPU
   is not bit-exact). The screenshots are not in the sources.
